      "value": "> This page documents the findings from the SFCC-128 spike. It covers the Global-e and Avalara AvaTax cartridge review conducted against the `zimmermann-sfcc` repository. Not approved for implementation until the sign-off in Section 6 is completed by the reviewer.\n\n---\n\nDocument Information\n--------------------\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Document ID** | TSD-SFCC-128 |\n| **Author(s)** | Victor Crisostomo, Squad-A |\n| **Reviewer(s)** | Victor Crisostomo |\n| **Created** | 23 Jul 2026 |\n| **Version** | v0.1 |\n| **Status** | Approved by @Victor T. Crisostomo |\n| **Related Jira** | SFCC-128 |\n\n---\n\nVersion History\n---------------\n\n| Version | Date | Summary of Change | Author |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| v0.1 | 23 Jul 2026 | Initial spike findings — cartridge inventory, integration analysis, and gap summary based on Victor's validation report and direct code review of `zimmermann-sfcc` repo | Victor Crisostomo |\n\n---\n\n1. Objective\n------------\n\nThe team was tasked with familiarising itself with the SFCC GitHub repository structure, with a focus on the existing third-party cartridges — specifically the **Global-e** (cross-border e-commerce) and **Avalara AvaTax** (tax calculation) cartridges — to understand how they are configured, how they integrate with the platform, and what customisation may be required before development begins.\n\n---\n\n2. Background\n-------------\n\nThe SFCC repository contains a number of pre-built and third-party cartridges that form the foundation of the build. Before development begins in earnest, the team needs a working understanding of:\n\n* What cartridges are present and what they do\n* How the cartridges are wired together across Zimmermann's multi-site setup\n* Where configuration changes, customisation, or gap remediation is needed\n\nVictor Crisostomo led a technical validation of the Global-e and Avalara cartridges against the repository on 16 July 2026, producing the `SFCC_GlobalE_AvaTax_Validation_Report.docx` (attached to SFCC-128 in Jira). This page summarises those findings. A detailed gap analysis is documented in the child page: **SFCC-131 — Global-e & AvaTax Gap Analysis**.\n\n---\n\n3. Cartridge Inventory\n----------------------\n\n### 3.1 Global-e Cartridges\n\n| Cartridge | Version | Purpose | Repo Path |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `int_globale` | v24.5.0 | Core business logic — Zimmermann override of vendor cartridge (hooks, jobs, scripts, factories, models) | `cartridges/int_globale` |\n| `int_globale_headless` | v24.5.0 | OCAPI/SCAPI headless hooks and JS SDK bootstrap (`GlobaleHeadless` controller) | `cartridges/int_globale_headless` |\n| `int_custom_zim_global` | v1.0.0 | Scaffold for Zimmermann-specific Global-e customisations — **currently empty** | `cartridges/int_custom_zim_global` |\n| `int_globale_sfra_popups` | v24.5.0 | Vendor SFRA popup templates and scripts | **Not present in repo** |\n\n### 3.2 AvaTax Cartridges\n\n| Cartridge | Purpose | Repo Path |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `int_avatax_svcclient` | AvaTax REST API v2 client — all transaction and address endpoints | `cartridges/int_avatax_svcclient` |\n| `int_avatax_sfra` | SFRA hook implementations: `calculateTax`, `createOrderNo`, BevAlc compliance | `cartridges/int_avatax_sfra` |\n| `bm_avatax` | Business Manager UI for AvaTax settings, certificate management, and reconciliation | `cartridges/bm_avatax` |\n\n### 3.3 Site Assignment (confirmed from `data/core/sites/*/site.xml`)\n\n| Integration | Sites |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Global-e** (`int_globale` + `int_globale_headless`) | ZimmermannEUIntl, ZimmermannUSIntl, ZimmermannME, ZimmermannHK |\n| **AvaTax** (`int_avatax_sfra` + `int_avatax_svcclient`) | ZimmermannAU, ZimmermannUS, ZimmermannEU, ZimmermannUK |\n\nAll 8 sites include `int_custom_zim_global` and `plugin_zim_scapi`.\n\n---\n\n4. Summary of Findings\n----------------------\n\nThe validation identified **13 configuration issues** across both integrations. Neither integration is ready to run in its current state — all service credentials are empty and AvaTax is only fully configured for ZimmermannAU.\n\n| Severity | Count | Key Issues |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **CRITICAL** | 4 | GE jobs target wrong site ID; AvaTax missing config for 3 of 4 sites; `buildTaxContent()` hardcoded test params; `commitTransactions: false` on all sites |\n| **HIGH** | 5 | All 25 GE service credentials empty; SFTP credential ID missing; SCAPI redirect URI defaults to localhost; merchant config placeholders; no GE site preferences in repo |\n| **MEDIUM** | 3 | BevAlc scope unconfirmed; `calculateTaxHelper.js` null reference risk in batch context; `int_globale_sfra_popups` absent from repo |\n| **LOW / INFO** | 3 | `int_custom_zim_global` is empty scaffold; LogEntries ID hardcoded; no automated tests |\n\nFull details — including required actions, file references, and open questions — are documented in the child page below.\n\n---\n\n5. Related Documentation\n------------------------\n\n* **Child page:** [FOR APPROVAL] SFCC-131 — Global-e & AvaTax Gap Analysis *(see below)*\n* **Jira:**[SFCC-128](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-128) — Spike parent ticket\n* **Jira:**[SFCC-131](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-131) — Gap analysis subtask\n* **Attachment:**`SFCC_GlobalE_AvaTax_Validation_Report.docx` — Victor Crisostomo, 16 Jul 2026 (attached to SFCC-128 in Jira)\n* **Related TSD:** TSD: Tax — SFCC & Avalara AvaTax\n* **Related page:** Global-E — Open Questions for SFCC / PWA Design\n\n---\n\n6. Sign-off\n-----------\n\n| Role | Name | Date | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Author | Victor Crisostomo | 23 Jul 2026 | Submitted |\n| Reviewer | Victor Crisostomo |  | Approved |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
