      "value": "> This page documents gaps, missing configuration, and customisation required for Zimmermann's Global-e and AvaTax SFCC setup. Based on Victor Crisostomo's validation report (16 Jul 2026) and direct code review of the `zimmermann-sfcc` repository. Not approved for implementation until the sign-off in Section 5 is completed by the reviewer.\n\n---\n\nDocument Information\n--------------------\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Document ID** | TSD-SFCC-131 |\n| **Author(s)** | Gideon Linsangan, Squad-B / Backend Developer |\n| **Reviewer(s)** | Victor Crisostomo |\n| **Created** | 23 Jul 2026 |\n| **Version** | v0.1 |\n| **Status** | Approved by @Victor T. Crisostomo |\n| **Related Jira** | SFCC-131 (subtask of SFCC-128) |\n\n---\n\nVersion History\n---------------\n\n| Version | Date | Summary of Change | Author |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| v0.1 | 23 Jul 2026 | Initial gap analysis — verified findings from Victor's validation report against direct code review; elevated `commitTransactions` to CRITICAL; added H-5 (no GE site preferences in repo) as a new finding | Gideon Linsangan |\n\n---\n\n1. Current State\n----------------\n\n### 1.1 Cartridge Inventory\n\n| Cartridge | Version | Purpose | Repo Path |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `int_globale` | v24.5.0 | Global-e core business logic (Zimmermann override) | `cartridges/int_globale` |\n| `int_globale_headless` | v24.5.0 | OCAPI/SCAPI hooks + JS SDK bootstrap | `cartridges/int_globale_headless` |\n| `int_custom_zim_global` | v1.0.0 | Zimmermann-specific GE customisation scaffold | `cartridges/int_custom_zim_global` |\n| `int_globale_sfra_popups` | — | Vendor popup templates | **Not present in repo** |\n| `int_avatax_svcclient` | — | AvaTax REST API v2 client | `cartridges/int_avatax_svcclient` |\n| `int_avatax_sfra` | — | SFRA hook implementations (calculateTax, createOrderNo, BevAlc) | `cartridges/int_avatax_sfra` |\n| `bm_avatax` | — | Business Manager UI (settings, certificate management) | `cartridges/bm_avatax` |\n\n### 1.2 Site Split (confirmed from `data/core/sites/*/site.xml`)\n\n**Global-e sites** — `int_globale` + `int_globale_headless` in cartridge path: - ZimmermannEUIntl, ZimmermannUSIntl, ZimmermannME, ZimmermannHK\n\n**AvaTax sites** — `int_avatax_sfra` + `int_avatax_svcclient` in cartridge path: - ZimmermannAU, ZimmermannUS, ZimmermannEU, ZimmermannUK\n\nAll 8 sites include `int_custom_zim_global` and `plugin_zim_scapi`.\n\n---\n\n2. Gaps & Required Configuration\n--------------------------------\n\n### 2.1 Critical\n\n---\n\n**C-1 — Global-e jobs target non-existent site** `RefArchGlobal` File: `data/vendor/globale-metadata/jobs.xml`\n\nAll 4 job definitions use `<context site-id=\"RefArchGlobal\"/>`: - `GlobaleSettings` (daily at 02:00 UTC) - `GlobaleProducts` (15-min delta sync, currently disabled) - `GlobaleOrderNotifications` (15-min, currently disabled) - `GlobaleCatalogFeed` (daily, currently disabled)\n\n`RefArchGlobal` does not exist in the Zimmermann site catalogue. If imported as-is, all jobs will fail at runtime because SFCC cannot resolve the site context.\n\n**Required action:** Replace `RefArchGlobal` with the correct Zimmermann site IDs for each job. Confirm with Global-e which site context the data sync jobs should target — typically a single primary site is sufficient if custom objects are organisation-scoped (see OQ-1).\n\n---\n\n**C-2 — AvaTax** `ATSettings` **missing for 3 of 4 AvaTax sites** File: `data/vendor/avalara-site-import/sites/ZimmermannAU/preferences.xml` (only file present)\n\nZimmermannAU has a properly configured `ATSettings`: - `companyCode: \"ZIMMERMANNWEARPTYLIMITED\"` ✓ - Ship-from: 115-151 Dunning Avenue, Sydney NSW 2018 ✓ - `commitTransactions: false` ← see C-4\n\nZimmermannUS, ZimmermannEU, and ZimmermannUK have **no site-specific ATSettings**. They fall back to the cartridge metadata default:\n\njsonwide760{\"companyCode\":\"default\",\"countryCode\":\"us\",\"taxationpolicy\":\"net\",\n\"line1\":\"\",\"city\":\"\",\"state\":\"\",\"zipCode\":\"\",\"commitTransactions\":false}\n\nThis means tax transactions from US/EU/UK are sent under `companyCode='default'`, the ship-from address is empty, and `countryCode:'us'` is hardcoded — wrong for ZimmermannEU and ZimmermannUK.\n\n**Required action:** Create `preferences.xml` under `data/vendor/avalara-site-import/sites/ZimmermannUS/`, `ZimmermannEU/`, and `ZimmermannUK/` with correct `ATSettings` JSON — correct `companyCode`, ship-from address, and `countryCode` per site (see OQ-2, OQ-3).\n\n---\n\n**C-3 —** `buildTaxContent()` **hardcodes test parameters, ignoring all caller arguments** File: `cartridges/int_avatax_svcclient/cartridge/scripts/avaTaxClient.js`, lines 295–298\n\nnonewide760function buildTaxContent(companyCode, documentDate, taxCodes, locationCodes) {\ndocumentDate = '2019-08-13'; // overwrites caller's argument\ncompanyCode = 'default'; // overwrites caller's argument\ntaxCodes = ['P0000000']; // overwrites caller's argument\nlocationCodes = ['NY', 'TN']; // overwrites caller's argument\n}\n\nAny caller passing valid Zimmermann company codes and location codes will have them silently replaced with 2019 test values. Tax content built by this function will always be attributed to `companyCode='default'` and US states NY/TN.\n\n**Required action:** Remove lines 295–298. Validate that callers pass correct arguments. Confirm with Avalara whether `buildTaxContent` is used by Zimmermann at all — if BevAlc is out of scope (see M-1), this function may be inactive.\n\n---\n\n**C-4 —** `commitTransactions: false` **on all AvaTax sites** File: `data/vendor/avalara-site-import/sites/ZimmermannAU/preferences.xml` and metadata default\n\n`commitTransactions` is `false` on ZimmermannAU and in the fallback default for all other sites. With this setting, AvaTax creates transactions in a `Saved` state — they do not appear in Avalara tax reports and do not generate tax remittance obligations. This breaks compliance reporting for all live sites simultaneously.\n\n> **Note:** Victor's report listed this as HIGH. Given that it blocks tax reporting across all sites, this has been elevated to CRITICAL here.\n\n**Required action:** Set `\"commitTransactions\": true` in ATSettings for all AvaTax sites once end-to-end testing is complete. Coordinate with Zimmermann's finance team on the go-live cutover date (see OQ-4).\n\n---\n\n### 2.2 High\n\n---\n\n**H-1 — All 25 Global-e service credentials are empty** File: `data/vendor/globale-metadata/services.xml`\n\nAll 25 `<service-credential>` entries have empty `<user-id/>` and `<password/>`. Browsing-endpoint credentials also contain path-only URLs with no base host. `Globale-OCAPI`, `Globale-SCAPI`, and SFTP credentials have empty URLs entirely.\n\n> The original report stated 24 credentials — the repo contains 25 (includes `Globale-UpdateParcelStatus`).\n\n**Required action:** Configure all 25 credentials in BM → Administration → Operations → Services. Global-e must supply base URL, API keys, and SFTP credentials. These cannot be stored in the repo — document in the project runbook.\n\n---\n\n**H-2 —** `Globale-SFTPUpload` **service has empty** `<credential-id/>` File: `data/vendor/globale-metadata/services.xml`, line 366\n\nThe `Globale-SFTPUpload` service has `<credential-id/>` (empty). SFCC cannot resolve the SFTP credential even after credentials are added to BM. The `GlobaleCatalogFeed` upload step will fail immediately.\n\n**Required action:** Set `<credential-id>` to the correct credential ID (likely `Globale-SFTPCatalogFeedUpload`) in the service definition, then re-import the services XML.\n\n---\n\n**H-3 —** `geSCAPIRedirectURI` **defaults to** `http://localhost:3000/callback` File: `data/vendor/globale-metadata/meta/system-objecttype-extensions.xml`, line 171\n\nThe `geSCAPIRedirectURI` site preference defaults to `http://localhost:3000/callback`. No site-specific overrides exist in the data import files. If SCAPI OAuth mode is active and this is not updated, OAuth flows will redirect to localhost and fail.\n\n**Required action:** Set `geSCAPIRedirectURI` per site in BM for each deployed environment (sandbox, staging, production). Add to the BM configuration runbook (see OQ-6).\n\n---\n\n**H-4 —** `avaMerchantConf.json` **contains only placeholder data** File: `cartridges/int_avatax_svcclient/cartridge/scripts/avaMerchantConf.json`\n\nBoth merchant entries (`merchantId-1`, `merchantId-2`) have empty `MerchantName`, `MerchantVatId`, and `MerchantEstablishmentCountry`. This file is loaded by `calculateTaxHelper.js` for merchant information in AvaTax transactions.\n\n**Required action:** Populate with Zimmermann's actual merchant details. Confirm with Avalara and legal whether multiple merchant IDs are required per site (see OQ-7).\n\n---\n\n**H-5 — No Global-e site preferences configured in repo**\n\nNo Global-e site-specific `preferences.xml` files exist under any Zimmermann site directory in the data imports. Preferences such as `geEnabled`, `geMerchantGUID`, `geEnvironment`, `geCountryCode`, and `gePaymentMethod` must be set per site in BM before Global-e can process any checkout.\n\n**Required action:** Document all required Global-e site preferences and their per-site values in the BM configuration runbook. Coordinate with Global-e to obtain `geMerchantGUID` and environment tokens for each site (see OQ-5).\n\n---\n\n### 2.3 Medium\n\n---\n\n**M-1 — BevAlc configuration contains placeholders; scope unconfirmed** File: `cartridges/int_avatax_svcclient/cartridge/scripts/avaBevAlcConf.json`\n\nBoth product entries are placeholders with all-empty BevAlc fields (`AlcoholContent`, `ContainerSize`, `Brand`, `taxCode`, etc.).\n\n**Required action:** Confirm with Zimmermann whether BevAlc compliance is required for any site (see OQ-8). If not required, confirm the BevAlc hooks in `int_avatax_sfra` are inactive. If required, supply real product IDs and alcohol attributes.\n\n---\n\n**M-2 —** `calculateTaxHelper.js` **reads** `customer.profile.taxID` **at module load time** File: `cartridges/int_avatax_sfra/cartridge/scripts/helpers/avatax/calculateTaxHelper.js`, line 28\n\nnonewide760var customerTaxId = !empty(customer.profile) ? customer.profile.taxID : null;\n\nThis executes at `require()` time outside any function scope. In batch job or pipeline contexts the `customer` implicit variable may not be available, resulting in a `ReferenceError` at module load.\n\n**Required action:** Move this assignment inside the function(s) that use `customerTaxId` so it is evaluated only in a valid request context.\n\n---\n\n**M-3 —** `int_globale_sfra_popups` **absent from repository**\n\nThe vendor popup template cartridge is not present in the repo and is not listed in any site's cartridge path. If country selector or welcome popup overlays are required, this cartridge needs to be added.\n\n**Required action:** Confirm with Global-e and Zimmermann UX whether the SFRA popup cartridge is needed in the headless/PWA context — it may be irrelevant if popups are handled by the PWA layer (see OQ-9).\n\n---\n\n### 2.4 Low / Info\n\n---\n\n**L-1 —** `int_custom_zim_global` **is an empty scaffold** File: `cartridges/int_custom_zim_global/`\n\nAll script directories contain only `.gitkeep` placeholder files. `steptypes.json` declares no step types. Currently has no functional impact but sits at the top of the cartridge path (highest override priority) for all 8 sites.\n\n**Required action:** Identify Zimmermann-specific overrides that should live here. Document explicitly that no GE customisations are in place until populated (see OQ-10).\n\n---\n\n**L-2 — LogEntries project ID hardcoded in** `avaTaxClient.js` File: `cartridges/int_avatax_svcclient/cartridge/scripts/avaTaxClient.js`, line 83\n\nnonewide760leUrl = leCredential.getURL() + 'a0n0b00000KU6CDAA1'; // logentries headless\n\nIf Zimmermann rotates the LogEntries token or moves to a different project, a code change is required.\n\n**Required action:** Move the project ID to a site preference or service credential URL (see OQ-11).\n\n---\n\n**L-3 — No automated tests for any Global-e or AvaTax cartridge script**\n\nThe `test/` directory contains no unit or integration tests covering `int_globale`, `int_globale_headless`, `int_avatax_sfra`, or `int_avatax_svcclient`.\n\n**Required action:** Not a blocker for initial launch. Track as a backlog item — at minimum, unit tests for `calculateTaxHelper.js` and `avaTaxClient.js` core functions would reduce regression risk.\n\n---\n\n3. Open Questions\n-----------------\n\n| # | Question | Owner | Priority |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| OQ-1 | Which Zimmermann site(s) should Global-e jobs target? Are custom objects org-level or site-scoped? | Global-e + SFCC Architect | CRITICAL |\n| OQ-2 | What are the correct Avalara company codes for ZimmermannUS, ZimmermannEU, and ZimmermannUK? | Zimmermann Finance / Avalara | CRITICAL |\n| OQ-3 | What are the correct ship-from addresses for US, EU, and UK warehouses/tax nexus points? | Zimmermann Ops | CRITICAL |\n| OQ-4 | When should `commitTransactions` be enabled? What is the go-live/cutover plan with Avalara? | Zimmermann Finance + Accenture | CRITICAL |\n| OQ-5 | Has Global-e provisioned Merchant GUIDs and API tokens for each of the 4 GE sites (EUIntl, USIntl, ME, HK)? | Global-e Account Manager | HIGH |\n| OQ-6 | Is SCAPI mode active on any site? If so, what are the correct `geSCAPIRedirectURI` values per environment? | SFCC Architect | HIGH |\n| OQ-7 | What Zimmermann merchant details (Name, VAT ID, establishment country) should populate `avaMerchantConf.json`? | Zimmermann Legal / Finance | HIGH |\n| OQ-8 | Is BevAlc (Beverage Alcohol compliance) required for any Zimmermann site? | Zimmermann Product | MEDIUM |\n| OQ-9 | Is `int_globale_sfra_popups` needed in the PWA/headless context? | Global-e + Zimmermann UX | MEDIUM |\n| OQ-10 | What Zimmermann-specific customisations are planned for `int_custom_zim_global`? | SFCC Architect | MEDIUM |\n| OQ-11 | Does Zimmermann use LogEntries/Rapid7 Insight for AvaTax logging? Confirm the project ID. | Zimmermann DevOps | LOW |\n\n---\n\n4. Summary Table\n----------------\n\n| Finding | Severity | Status | Action Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| C-1: GE jobs target `RefArchGlobal` | CRITICAL | Open | Update `jobs.xml` with correct Zimmermann site IDs |\n| C-2: ATSettings missing for US/EU/UK | CRITICAL | Open | Create per-site `preferences.xml` imports |\n| C-3: `buildTaxContent()` hardcoded params | CRITICAL | Open | Remove 4 hardcoded override lines |\n| C-4: `commitTransactions: false` everywhere | CRITICAL | Open | Enable after end-to-end testing |\n| H-1: 25 GE service credentials empty | HIGH | Open | Configure in BM; document in runbook |\n| H-2: `Globale-SFTPUpload` missing `credential-id` | HIGH | Open | Fix `services.xml`, re-import |\n| H-3: `geSCAPIRedirectURI` → localhost | HIGH | Open | Set per-site in BM per environment |\n| H-4: `avaMerchantConf.json` placeholders | HIGH | Open | Populate with real merchant data |\n| H-5: No GE site preferences in repo | HIGH | Open | Configure per-site in BM; add to runbook |\n| M-1: BevAlc config placeholders / scope unclear | MEDIUM | Open | Confirm scope with Zimmermann |\n| M-2: `customer.profile.taxID` at module load | MEDIUM | Open | Move inside function scope |\n| M-3: `int_globale_sfra_popups` absent | MEDIUM | Open | Confirm if needed; obtain from vendor if so |\n| L-1: `int_custom_zim_global` is empty | LOW/INFO | Open | Define customisation requirements |\n| L-2: LogEntries ID hardcoded | LOW | Open | Move to config/preference |\n| L-3: No automated tests | LOW | Backlog | Create unit tests post-launch |\n\n---\n\n5. Sign-off\n-----------\n\n| Role | Name | Date | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Author | Gideon Linsangan | 23 Jul 2026 | Submitted |\n| Reviewer | Victor Crisostomo |  | Approved |\n\n---\n\n*Document prepared as deliverable for SFCC-131. Based on Victor Crisostomo's validation report (16 Jul 2026) and direct code review of the* `zimmermann-sfcc` *repository. Last updated: 23 Jul 2026.*",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f4cb",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

